Yes. Rotation is one of civilization’s favorite carriers of work because it is continuous, recirculating, compact, ratio-adjustable, and easy to store as momentum. But beneath rotation is the deeper pattern:

We capture asymmetry before it dissipates.

Wind, falling water, heat, pressure, voltage, tension, chemical potential, attention, disagreement, and desire are all differences trying to equalize. A machine inserts itself into that equalization and makes the passage perform useful work.

difference → constrained path → directed flow → transduction → useful work + residual

That is a major Pantheon extension because the repository already treats the durable unit as an operator that survives translation, and already contains Gear, Bearing, Differential, Clutch, Ratchet, Gyro, and Governor Seals.  This expands those parts into a complete machine grammar.

